    <!-- Chrome -->
    <string name="yahtzee_help_title">How to Play Yahtzee</string>
    <string name="yahtzee_help_body">Each turn you roll five dice up to three times. After a roll, tap the dice you want to keep; the others are rerolled. Then fill one scoring box with the dice you end up with.\n\nUpper section: Aces to Sixes score the total of that number. Reach 63 or more in the upper section for a 35 point bonus.\n\nLower section: Three of a kind and Four of a kind score the total of all five dice. Full house is 25, Small straight (four in a row) 30, Large straight (five in a row) 40, Yahtzee (five alike) 50, and Chance is the total of all dice.\n\nEvery box is used once, so sometimes you have to take a zero. A second Yahtzee after you scored 50 earns a 100 point bonus and must go in the matching upper box, or in any lower box if that one is taken (the Joker rule).\n\nA game lasts 13 rounds. Undo takes back a hold or a box choice until the next roll.</string>
    <string name="yahtzee_leave_title">Leave this game?</string>
